# I found no shift of sense. In both S4 and S5, "die" and "death" mean the ending of life, and "all things... at last" means the eventual death of everything.
# A1 links the dead not returning to the living coming from something other than the dead. Both claims keep the same sense of life and death, so A1 does not act as a bridge.
